static const char _zs214_d[] = "private escape\n\nA `.private` view may only be taken by the value's own type, or by a holder of an existing `.private` handle (a friend the type passed it to). External code holding only a public value cannot produce one.";
static const z_t81_t _zs214 = { .data = _zs214_d, .size = 220 };
static const char _zs215_d[] = "ownership error\n\nA value's ownership was used incorrectly: used after a take/move, a borrow outliving its lock, a reftype aliased while locked, or a reassignment in another mode than the name was bound with -- an owned name takes an owned value (`x = d.take`), a borrow is re-pointed (`b = d`). See docs/ownership.";
